> back at four different letters again? ;-)

Is that a distinction the average caveman or naive tourist would notice?

Restrict the classes to creatures that look obviously different.
Being humanoid, the adventurer will have no trouble with fine
distinctions amonst fellow humanoids - so elves, dwarves, orcs
all get a letter despite looking much the same - but the difference
between a pudding and a jelly would be lost on them.

The freed letters could be used for more categories of demons, or
of humanoids.

